issue_comments.body:
@hao-aaron Agreed: padding belongs to #64352. I removed it from this PR in `4ee8f3a41f`:
- `begin_direct_reload` is back to `t.data = view  # no zeroing: ...`;
- `test_direct_reload_zeroes_padding` is gone. It wrote `param.data` directly and depended on the zero, as you noted;
- `_moe`'s `intermediate_size` override is reverted.

The `mxfp4-marlin` case of `test_direct_reload_keeps_kernel_tensor_addresses` stays. It loads the full parameters, checks that Marlin MXFP4 keeps its tensor addresses, and passes without the zero.

Until #64352 lands, gpt-oss on `--moe-backend marlin` therefore still fails a direct reload on this branch (0.43 → 0.00), as on main.

Unit tests on the new head (GB300, slurm 21994): `test_keep_param_objects.py`, `test_utils.py` and `test_direct_reload.py`, 100 passed, 1 skipped (SM90-only W4A8).

